                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued November 18 at 1:53PM PST until November 19 at 6:00PM PST by NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Los Angeles County.\n\n* WHEN...From Thursday morning through Thursday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive rainfall may result in significant flooding of\nroads and other low-lying areas, heavy flows in creeks and canyons,\nrockslides, mudslides, and debris flows in recent burn scars.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Rain rates up to 1 inch per hour are expected, especially in the\nmountains.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
